## Project Overview
A web-based truck queue management system designed for operators and staff. Initially implemented with **pure HTML, CSS, and JS** for lightweight use in browsers. Later duplicated and migrated to **Electron** for easier installation.

Uses Dual Monitor, should still work without second monitor

> [GitHub](https://github.com/YolkFinggers/truckQueue)

---

## Development Timeline & Key Decisions

### Phase 1: Initial Web App (Lite Version)
- Built using **pure HTML, CSS, JS** (no SDK used).  
- Relied on **user’s own browser** to run.  
- Features implemented:
  - Display truck queue, assigned loading bay with no status and failed to reach loading bay
  - Basic add truck form.
  - Queue table in assign.html for operators with "Mark Failed" and "Reached" button.

- **Notes:**
  - No SDK, lightweight and portable.
  - End-users only needed a browser to use the app but....
  - Setup included a `.bat` script for auto-start on Windows, **MUST HAVE** Google Chrome installed.

---

### Phase 2: Electron Transition
- Duplicated/migrated the web app to **Electron** for better desktop integration.  
- Goals of this Electron version:
  - Support both on Linux & Windows
  - Multi-monitor support without relying on any pre-installed browser.
  - Simplify setting up auto-start web app on device startup

- **Challenges & Solutions:**
  - Startup issues: Ensured Electron executes the entirety of the app correctly via `.exe`.
  - Build errors: Resolved symbolic link permissions by running CMD as admin.
  - File packaging: Decided to upload only `.exe` in releases; Linux/unpacked files are large and without extension.

---

## Notes on Technology & Setup
- **Electron**: Main platform for all future development.  
- **Google**: Only needed if not using Electron
- **Distribution**: GitHub releases with `.exe` packaged; end-users don’t need to install anything beyond this.  

---

